From: Yugen <19thkingisreal@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dictBuilder: fix displayLevel being zeroed before use

COVER_ctx_init() and FASTCOVER_ctx_init() both assign ctx->displayLevel
from the caller's notification level and then memset() the whole context
to zero a few lines later. Every diagnostic that reads back
ctx->displayLevel therefore sees 0 and is silently suppressed, at any -v
level.

Concretely, this disables the dictionary builder's progress reporting in
COVER_buildDictionary()/FASTCOVER_buildDictionary(), including:

    "Breaking content into %u epochs of size %u\n"
    "Constructed dictionary of size %u\n"

Those two lines are the only user-visible signal of the builder's epoch
geometry and of how much of --maxdict was actually filled, so a build
that terminates early (zero-score run) and emits a dictionary much
smaller than requested currently does so with no output whatsoever, even
at -vvvv.

Diagnostics emitted directly inside *_ctx_init() are unaffected, because
the DISPLAYLEVEL macro captures the local variable and the function
parameter is still in scope there; only the read-back through the context
is broken. This is why the bug is easy to miss.

Fix: perform the assignment after the memset.

Signed-off-by: Yugen <19thkingisreal@gmail.com>
---
 lib/dictBuilder/cover.c     | 3 ++-
 lib/dictBuilder/fastcover.c | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/dictBuilder/cover.c b/lib/dictBuilder/cover.c
index 1234567..89abcde 100644
--- a/lib/dictBuilder/cover.c
+++ b/lib/dictBuilder/cover.c
@@ -636,7 +636,6 @@ static size_t COVER_ctx_init(COVER_ctx_t *ctx, const void *samplesBuffer,
   const size_t trainingSamplesSize = splitPoint < 1.0 ? COVER_sum(samplesSizes, nbTrainSamples) : totalSamplesSize;
   const size_t testSamplesSize = splitPoint < 1.0 ? COVER_sum(samplesSizes + nbTrainSamples, nbTestSamples) : totalSamplesSize;
-  ctx->displayLevel = displayLevel;
   /* Checks */
   if (totalSamplesSize < MAX(d, sizeof(U64)) ||
       totalSamplesSize >= (size_t)COVER_MAX_SAMPLES_SIZE) {
@@ -656,6 +655,8 @@ static size_t COVER_ctx_init(COVER_ctx_t *ctx, const void *samplesBuffer,
   }
   /* Zero the context */
   memset(ctx, 0, sizeof(*ctx));
+  /* Must come after the memset, which would otherwise clear it */
+  ctx->displayLevel = displayLevel;
   DISPLAYLEVEL(2, "Training on %u samples of total size %u\n", nbTrainSamples,
                (unsigned)trainingSamplesSize);
   DISPLAYLEVEL(2, "Testing on %u samples of total size %u\n", nbTestSamples,
diff --git a/lib/dictBuilder/fastcover.c b/lib/dictBuilder/fastcover.c
index 1234567..89abcde 100644
--- a/lib/dictBuilder/fastcover.c
+++ b/lib/dictBuilder/fastcover.c
@@ -317,7 +317,6 @@ FASTCOVER_ctx_init(FASTCOVER_ctx_t* ctx, const void* samplesBuffer,
     const size_t trainingSamplesSize = splitPoint < 1.0 ? FASTCOVER_sum(samplesSizes, nbTrainSamples) : totalSamplesSize;
     const size_t testSamplesSize = splitPoint < 1.0 ? FASTCOVER_sum(samplesSizes + nbTrainSamples, nbTestSamples) : totalSamplesSize;
-    ctx->displayLevel = displayLevel;
     /* Checks */
     if (totalSamplesSize < MAX(d, sizeof(U64)) ||
         totalSamplesSize >= (size_t)FASTCOVER_MAX_SAMPLES_SIZE) {
@@ -341,6 +340,8 @@ FASTCOVER_ctx_init(FASTCOVER_ctx_t* ctx, const void* samplesBuffer,
     }
     /* Zero the context */
     memset(ctx, 0, sizeof(*ctx));
+    /* Must come after the memset, which would otherwise clear it */
+    ctx->displayLevel = displayLevel;
     DISPLAYLEVEL(2, "Training on %u samples of total size %u\n", nbTrainSamples,
                  (unsigned)trainingSamplesSize);
     DISPLAYLEVEL(2, "Testing on %u samples of total size %u\n", nbTestSamples,
